Note: If I(xi) ~ C * xi for large xi, then -log|D_N| ~ C * N * xi = (C / kappa) * r,
providing strong numerical evidence for an N-scaled large-deviation form and,
if I(xi) becomes asymptotically linear, evidence for an exponential-in-r envelope.

